# NOTE: the .NET template excludes **/charts here, meaning Helm charts. This
# repository has none, and it does have web/src/components/charts — which
# the pattern would silently remove from the build context, so the exclusion
# stays deleted.
**/docker-compose*
**/Dockerfile*
**/node_modules
**/npm-debug.log
**/obj
**/wwwroot
**/secrets.dev.yaml
**/values.dev.yaml
LICENSE
README.md

# Sync-conflict copies. iCloud and Dropbox resolve a clash by writing
# "name 2.ext" beside the original. These have broken the Docker build once by
# shadowing a real directory, and a copy of .env would not be matched by the
# rule above — so they are excluded by name here as well.
* 2
* 2.*

# Next.js build outputs; the image builds its own.
web/.next
web/out

# The development settings hold a keypair and a signing key. Production
# overrides both through the environment, so this file is only ever read on a
# laptop — but `dotnet publish` copies every appsettings*.json into the output,
# so without this the file rides inside every image anybody pulls.
**/appsettings.Development.json
